  "text": "ordinarium.praefatio-communis",
  "about": "The Common Preface names no mystery of the day. After “through Christ our Lord” it turns to the angelic choirs' praise of God. Its opening sentence is built around “est”, which governs the construction “nos tibi grátias ágere”.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "narrative": "The priest parts his hands and holds them apart to the end of the Preface." },
    "s02": { "translation": "Truly it is right and just, fitting and leading to salvation, that we should give You thanks always and everywhere:" },
    "s03": { "translation": "Holy Lord, almighty Father, eternal God: through Christ our Lord.", "translation_citations": [{ "title": "The Family Prayer-book (1839)", "locator": "p. 79", "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_family_prayer-book,_containing_all_the_public_and_private_devotions_in_use_amongst_English_Catholics._(IA_TheFamilyPrayerBookContaining).pdf" }] },
    "s04": { "translation": "Through Him the Angels praise Your majesty, the Dominions adore it, and the Powers tremble before it.", "translation_citations": [{ "title": "The Family Prayer-book (1839)", "locator": "p. 79", "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_family_prayer-book,_containing_all_the_public_and_private_devotions_in_use_amongst_English_Catholics._(IA_TheFamilyPrayerBookContaining).pdf" }] },
    "s05": { "translation": "The heavens, the heavenly Virtues, and the blessed Seraphim join in joyful celebration of Your majesty.", "translation_citations": [{ "title": "The Family Prayer-book (1839)", "locator": "p. 79", "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_family_prayer-book,_containing_all_the_public_and_private_devotions_in_use_amongst_English_Catholics._(IA_TheFamilyPrayerBookContaining).pdf" }] },
    "s06": { "translation": "We beseech You to admit our voices to join theirs as we speak in humble confession:" }
  },
